const MODE_INFO={summary:['One short page that covers the most important rules from all six rule sets.','A compact file. The AI gets the key do\'s and don\'ts without long examples, so it reads your project details sooner.','You want a quick start, use a free or smaller AI plan, or paste into a chat with a size limit.'],paired:['The one-page summary, plus the full rule set for each topic your chosen steps touch. Untick steps and fewer sets are added.','A medium file. Stricter, more detailed guidance exactly where your steps need it, such as writing rules for research steps and code rules for build steps.','You want better results on the parts you\'re building without the full weight of every rule.'],full:['All six rule sets in full, with every rule and every example: core rules, visual design, writing, sounding human, layout and mobile, and code quality.','The largest file. The most thorough guidance and the fewest generic results, but it takes up more of the AI\'s memory.','You\'re handing off a whole project, use a tool with lots of room (like Claude or Cursor), or want the strictest review.']};
const FAQ=[["start","Getting started",[["What is this site?","A free collection of 25 ready-made instructions (called prompts) for AI tools like Claude, ChatGPT and Cursor. Together they take a website or app from first research to launch. It also includes anti-slop rules that stop the AI from giving you generic, look-alike results."],["Do I need to know how to code?","No. The questions are in plain language and most steps produce plans, wording and design decisions. A few steps produce code; you can hand those to a developer or ask the AI to explain them."],["Which AI tools does it work with?","Any AI you chat with: Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini, Cursor, Copilot Chat and others. Everything is plain text, so it pastes anywhere."],["Is it free? Can I use it for client work?","Yes. Everything is under the MIT licence, so you can use, copy and change it, including for paid and commercial projects."],["Where should I start?","Building a whole project? Use the Workflow page. Need help with one task, like writing button labels or checking colour contrast? Pick a single prompt from the library.","Open the prompt library","#/prompts"]]],["workflow","Using the workflow",[["What does the Workflow page actually do?","It turns your answers into one file. That file holds all 25 steps in the right order, with your project details already filled in and the anti-slop rules attached. You paste it into an AI once instead of 25 times.","Go to the workflow","#/workflow"],["Which questions do I have to answer?","Only three: the project name, a short description, and what you are building. Everything else is optional. Anything you leave blank, the AI will ask you about when it gets there."],["What are \"shared answers\"?","Details that several steps need, like your industry or your audience. You type them once and every step that needs them is filled in automatically."],["Can I skip steps?","Yes. Untick any step in the list of 25 and it is left out of your file. The file, the progress bar and the checks update straight away."],["My framework is not in the list. What do I do?","Type its name under \"Choose a framework\" and press Add framework. It is saved on this device and you can remove it with the × button. If you are unsure, pick \"Not sure\" and the AI will recommend one."],["Can I attach files instead of typing?","Yes, in step 06 (real content) and step 07 (design direction). Text files like .md, .txt or .csv go into your file in full. Images and PDFs are listed by name, so attach those in your AI chat when you paste. You can add up to 10 files per step."],["What do the personality settings mean?","Three dials from 1 (calm) to 3 (bold). Energy is how striking the design feels, Rhythm is how much sections vary from one another, and Motion is how much things move. The middle setting suits most products."]]],["rules","Anti-slop rules",[["What is \"AI slop\"?","The tell-tale signs of lazy AI output: buzzwords like \"seamless\" and \"revolutionary\", the same purple gradients on every site, vague buttons that say \"Learn more\", and code that looks fine but breaks. The rules list these patterns so the AI avoids them.","Read the rules","#/antislop"],["Which rules option should I choose?","Combined summary suits most people: one short page with the key rules. Summary plus paired files adds detail where your steps need it. All six files is the strictest and longest. On the Workflow page, the (i) button next to the options compares them side by side."],["What do the pass and check labels mean?","As you type, your file is checked against the rules. Pass means that rule is met. Check means something needs a look, such as a buzzword in your description. Em dashes are fixed for you; everything else is yours to rewrite."]]],["file","Your file and the AI",[["How do I use the file once I have it?","Press Copy and paste it into a new AI chat, or Download and attach the .md file. Then type \"start\". The AI works through one step at a time and asks before moving on."],["The AI says my file is too long.","Pick Combined summary for the rules, untick steps you do not need, or work one step at a time with the \"Copy this step only\" button inside each step."],["What are the words in [BRACKETS] in a prompt?","Spaces for your own details, like [INDUSTRY_TYPE]. On the Workflow page they are filled in from your answers. When you copy a single prompt from the library, replace them yourself or use the fill-in form on that prompt's page."]]],["site","Privacy and the site",[["Is my information saved or sent anywhere?","It is saved only in this browser, on this device, so you can come back later. Nothing is uploaded to a server. Clearing your browser data, or using a private window, erases it."],["How do I start over?","On the Workflow page, press \"Clear all answers\" at the bottom of the \"Your workflow file\" panel."],["Can I change the text size or use dark mode?","Yes. Open the Display menu at the top of any page to switch between light and dark, and to make the text larger."],["Does it work on a phone?","Yes. Every page works on small screens. For long projects a larger screen is more comfortable, and your answers are saved on whichever device you use."],["What do the Beta and Under revision labels mean?","They mark prompts that are still being improved. They work, but the wording may change. Each prompt page explains its status."]]]];
const MODES=[['summary','Combined summary','All rules on one page. Fastest to paste.'],['paired','Summary plus paired skill files','Adds the full skill file each included folder needs.'],['full','All six files in full','Every rule and example. Largest file.']];
const shiftH=(t,n)=>{let f=false;return t.split('\n').map(l=>{if(/^\s*```/.test(l)){f=!f;return l}if(!f){const m=l.match(/^(#{1,6}) /);if(m)return '#'.repeat(Math.min(6,m[1].length+n))+l.slice(m[1].length)}return l}).join('\n')};
